1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:01,580
It's freezing outside.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,610
So how can that
air heat your home?

3
00:00:04,287 --> 00:00:05,987
Even freezing air holds heat.

4
00:00:06,407 --> 00:00:07,834
Zero Celsius is still

5
00:00:07,954 --> 00:00:09,509
far above absolute zero.

6
00:00:10,549 --> 00:00:12,639
A heat pump moves
that heat indoors,

7
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:14,992
with refrigerant
circling a sealed loop.

8
00:00:15,962 --> 00:00:18,273
Outside, refrigerant
colder than the air

9
00:00:18,356 --> 00:00:20,831
soaks up its heat
and boils into a gas.

10
00:00:21,691 --> 00:00:23,341
A compressor squeezes the gas,

11
00:00:23,551 --> 00:00:25,071
and its temperature shoots up.

12
00:00:25,791 --> 00:00:28,338
Indoors, the hot gas
releases that heat

13
00:00:28,401 --> 00:00:30,831
into your home and
condenses to a liquid.

14
00:00:31,661 --> 00:00:34,054
An expansion valve
drops the pressure, the

15
00:00:34,106 --> 00:00:36,456
liquid goes cold,
and the loop repeats.

16
00:00:37,516 --> 00:00:39,136
Moving heat beats making it.

17
00:00:39,418 --> 00:00:40,688
You usually get more heat

18
00:00:40,688 --> 00:00:41,970
out than electricity in.
